            <div xml:id="d7">

                <pb facs="0129" n="5" xml:id="pg5"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/10934a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wallace</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-01-28T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 28,
                                1921—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>62. If you can informally arrange to be given copies of minutes of meetings of
                    Conference of Ambassadors it would be of great value to the Department to
                    continue to receive them. Telegraphic summaries are unnecessary except of
                    discussions important to the United States.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
